<% content_for :title, 'Starmap Display' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Starmap Display' do %>
  <div class='space-y-8'>

    <p class='text-fg-muted'>
      The gear icon on the interactive starmap opens the Map Display dialogue. Choices made there are
      stored in your browser for this campaign and apply only to you.
    </p>

    <div>
      <p class=' uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-highlight-fg mb-4'>Jump Log</p>

      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Display</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            How the ship&rsquo;s recorded jumps are drawn. <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Fill</span>
            colours each hex the ship has visited, <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Line</span> draws a
            line from the origin hex to the destination hex of every jump,
            <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Fill and line</span> does both, and
            <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>None</span> hides the jump log.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Fill Colour</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The colour of visited hexes. Shown when the display includes a fill.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Line Colour, Style and Width</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The appearance of the jump lines, set the same way as for jump routes: a colour, a style
            (solid, dashed, dotted and so on) and a width from 1 to 20. Shown when the display includes a line.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Campaign Defaults</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Until you change a value, the starmap uses the referee&rsquo;s campaign setting for it. Once you
            change a value, yours always takes precedence, even if the referee later changes the campaign
            setting. <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Use campaign defaults</span> discards all of
            your jump log choices at once.
          </dd>
        </div>

      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class=' uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-highlight-fg mb-4'>Jump Log Table</p>

      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Viewing</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The arrow icon in the starmap navigation bar opens the jump log: every recorded jump, newest first,
            showing the ship, the date it departed and the origin, then the date it arrived and the destination. A misjump is marked beside its
            destination. Anyone viewing the campaign can read the table, and the Ship selector above it narrows the list to one
            vessel.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Adding and Editing</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            The referee sees an <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Add jump</span> button and a pencil
            icon on each row to edit it. If a ship is selected in the table, Add jump starts with that ship. Choosing a ship fills in its
            last known position and departure date, and the arrival date follows the departure by seven days.
            The destination sector and hex lists offer only places within the ship&rsquo;s jump rating of its origin
            (4 if the ship has no rating), unless the jump is marked as a misjump.
            Unless the jump is a misjump, the arrival must be at least six days after the departure, and the
            departure cannot be earlier than the ship&rsquo;s previous arrival. The form shows the earliest departure and arrival
            allowed and will not accept earlier dates. A misjump may arrive on any date.
            Editing a jump adjusts the neighbouring jumps of the same ship so the log stays continuous, and the
            lines on the map are redrawn once the change is saved.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Deleting</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            A ship&rsquo;s most recent jump also has a bin icon. Selecting it asks you to
            confirm before anything is removed. Only a ship&rsquo;s most recent jump can be deleted; its earlier
            jumps can be edited but not removed.
          </dd>
        </div>

      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='iiss-form'>
      REFERENCE 0709SD
    </div>

  </div>
<% end %>
